-    // ---- fishpond patch 85: a tutor is worth what it finds (the user, 2026-10-21) ----
-    // "Score the tutor as whatever the choice is, + the cost of casting the tutor itself ... if it goes to hand (or top
-    // library), the cost of the tutor is added to the cost of the spell when it's weighing whether to cast the tutor. If it goes
-    // to battlefield, like in Natural Order, the casting cost is replaced with the tutor's cost." The plan valued a tutor as
-    // any spell of its mana value (Diabolic Tutor 160 against 228 for the plays it made) and held tutors for turns
-    // (bracket1000_20261021: Wilson's Idyllic Tutor and Open the Armory 28 streaks each, Diabolic Tutor 22, Demonic 17).
-    //  - the pick: what the harness's pilot policy would fetch (TUTOR_RANK), else Forge's own pick; its value is the plan's own
-    //    value of casting it now (a win, an engine, the setup model's ramp all count)
-    //  - to hand: worth the pick, planned only when the tutor and the pick fit this turn's mana (cost = the tutor's + the
-    //    pick's, so the pick is cast after it); to the top of the library: the same against next turn's mana, costing the
-    //    tutor's now and the draw it replaces; onto the battlefield: worth the pick at the tutor's cost (X tutors: the pick's
-    //    mana value, planned last since Forge pays X with what's left); a sacrifice it costs takes the cheapest creature off
-    //  - a creature or permanent that tutors when it enters (Recruiter of the Guard) adds the pick to its own value
-    //  - when the pair doesn't fit, the tutor keeps its old value: never planned less than before
