+    // ---- fishpond patch 85: a tutor is worth what it finds (the user, 2026-10-21) ----
+    // "Score the tutor as whatever the choice is, + the cost of casting the tutor itself ... if it goes to hand (or top
+    // library), the cost of the tutor is added to the cost of the spell when it's weighing whether to cast the tutor. If it goes
+    // to battlefield, like in Natural Order, the casting cost is replaced with the tutor's cost." The plan valued a tutor as
+    // any spell of its mana value (Diabolic Tutor 160 against 228 for the plays it made) and held tutors for turns
+    // (bracket1000_20261021: Wilson's Idyllic Tutor and Open the Armory 28 streaks each, Diabolic Tutor 22, Demonic 17).
+    //  - the pick: what the harness's pilot policy would fetch (TUTOR_RANK), else Forge's own pick; its value is the plan's own
+    //    value of casting it now (a win, an engine, the setup model's ramp all count)
+    //  - to hand: worth the pick, planned only when the tutor and the pick fit this turn's mana (cost = the tutor's + the
+    //    pick's, so the pick is cast after it); to the top of the library: the same against next turn's mana, costing the
+    //    tutor's now and the draw it replaces; onto the battlefield: worth the pick at the tutor's cost (X tutors: the pick's
+    //    mana value, planned last since Forge pays X with what's left); a sacrifice it costs takes the cheapest creature off
+    //  - a creature or permanent that tutors when it enters (Recruiter of the Guard) adds the pick to its own value
+    //  - when the pair doesn't fit, the tutor keeps its old value: never planned less than before
+    // Land tutors stay ramp (the setup model). -Dfishpond.tutorValue=false turns it off.
+
+    // ---- fishpond patch 89: a card a tutor put near the top of the library (the user, 2026-10-22: "These tutors, especially
+    // Long Term Plans, is a trap for an AI like this"). Zur's game 0 (zur5b_20261022): Long-Term Plans put Approach of the
+    // Second Sun third from the top, then Zur's attack search shuffled it away; later Personal Tutor and Mystical Tutor both
+    // fetched Approach to the top in one turn. While a tutored card waits in the top three: nothing that searches (and so
+    // shuffles) the seat's own library is played or planned (Zur's optional trigger is declined; Wizardcycling is a tutor too),
+    // a draw that reaches it is worth that card, and a top-of-library tutor's value counts the draws it waits for. ----
+    /** The card a pilot seat's own tutor last put into its library (set by the harness's search choice). */
+    public static final Map<Player, Card> TOP = Collections.synchronizedMap(new WeakHashMap<>());
+
+    static final Set<Integer> PLACED = Collections.synchronizedSet(new HashSet<>());   // tutored cards seen in their place
+
+    /** That card, while it is still among the top three of its owner's library (a shuffle or a draw ends it). It is recorded
+     *  when chosen, before the tutor moves it, so it only expires once it has been seen in place (zur5c_20261022 game 0:
+     *  checked mid-resolution, Long-Term Plans' Approach was dropped and Zur's search shuffled it away). */
+    public static Card knownTop(final Player p) {
+        // the real game only: a lookahead copy's player equals the real one as a map key, and its simulated search shuffled the
+        // copy's library and wiped the real entry (zur5c_20261022 game 0: Zur's trigger, simulated in main 1)
+        final Card c = p == null || !real(p.getGame()) ? null : TOP.get(p);
+        if (c == null) {
+            return null;
+        }
+        final int i = knownTopIndex(p, c);
+        if (i < 0 || i > 2) {
+            if (PLACED.remove(c.getId()) || !inLibrary(p, c)) TOP.remove(p);   // shuffled away, drawn, or gone
+            return null;
+        }
+        PLACED.add(c.getId());
+        return p.getCardsIn(ZoneType.Library).get(i);
