+    // ---- fishpond patch 95: a spell lock (zur300_20261023 game 55: under Zur's own Rule of Law the plan cast Sol Ring first,
+    // worth 125, and Archaeomancer, worth 1256 as the loop's missing piece, couldn't be cast that turn; two Triskaidekaphile
+    // draws spent the mana instead). Under "each player can't cast more than N spells each turn" (Rule of Law, Arcane
+    // Laboratory; Deafening Silence counts noncreature spells) a set holds no more spells than the lock still allows (the
+    // best set by value, as always), and a spell outside the plan isn't cast while the plan's spells need the cast.
+    // Abilities (cycling, Wizardcycling, activations) are never limited. ----
+    /** fishpond patch 99: a "no more than N spells each turn" lock applies to p (Rule of Law). */
+    public static boolean spellLimited(final Player p) {
+        final int[] lim = spellsLeft(p);
+        return lim[0] >= 0 || lim[1] >= 0;
+    }
